# The Netlify CLI deploys this FOLDER, not the git tree — .gitignore has no
# say in what ships. That is how 134 MB of raw Meshy exports and every
# unedited photograph ended up publicly downloadable from the live site:
# storeurbannest.netlify.app/models/source/crystal chandelier-raw.glb was
# serving 106 MB to anyone who asked for it.
#
# Keep this file in step with .gitignore. The two do different jobs — one
# keeps things out of the repo, this one keeps them off the CDN.

# Working photographs. Only the cropped WebP files sitting directly in
# images/ ship; every subfolder is material we edited from.
images/*/

# Raw Meshy exports. Only the compressed .glb in models/ has any business
# being served, and even those are now fetched from Supabase Storage.
models/source/

# Local tooling — the compression script, its lockfile, the render check.
tools/

# Editor and agent configuration.
.claude/

# Never the raw project files.
*.blend
*.fbx
*.obj
